  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 260353,
  "projectUrl": "https://vegarise.com/Products/VDocs",
  "published": "2026-02-06T00:46:19.11Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes\n🚀 Version: 2026.1.3\n\nPublic API Improvements\n✨ What’s New!!!\n🧾 This release focuses on refining and improving the public APIs to make VegaDoc more intuitive, consistent, and easier to use when building and manipulating documents.\n🔧 Improvements\n\n - Refined public DOM APIs\n\n  - Simplified access patterns for core document elements\n\n  - Improved naming consistency across DOM abstractions\n\n  - Clearer separation between document structure and rendering concerns\n\n- Enhanced section abstraction\n\n  - Better exposure of section-level features such as headers, footers, page setup, and layout behavior\n\n  - Improved API consistency for adding and managing sections\n\n- Improved page and layout configuration APIs\n\n  - Clearer and more discoverable APIs for page settings, margins, orientation, and background behavior\n\n  - Better alignment with Word document concepts while keeping the API format-agnostic\n\n- More predictable object model behavior\n\n  - Reduced ambiguity when working with child elements (sections, pages, headers, footers)\n\n  - Improved safety checks and validation in public-facing methods\n\n📚 Developer Experience\n\n- Improved XML documentation for public APIs\n\n- Better IntelliSense guidance when working in IDEs\n\n- APIs are now easier to understand without requiring deep knowledge of WordprocessingML\n\n⚠️ Notes\n\n- This release may include minor breaking changes if you relied on undocumented or internal behaviors.\n\n- No changes are required for typical usage scenarios, but reviewing the updated APIs is recommended.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "VDocs - Word Document Framework",
